readability and maintenance of tests. By using these interfaces, you can test code paths that may throw exceptions, validate inputs, and ensure timely execution of operations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/dd8f845c3932503930e3f5c8550cfa3e?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":8,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-07-11T13:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"s7KBr3qnz","title":"Getting started with Spring Security and JWT","url":"https://reflectoring.io/spring-security-jwt/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/getting-started-with-spring-security-and-jwt-s7kbr3qnz","summary":"Spring Security offers robust security features for Java applications, including session management, authentication, and protection against common threats like CSRF. This guide covers the implementation of JWT (JSON Web Token) for secure communication between two parties. JWTs are versatile and can be used for single sign-on, API authentication, stateless sessions, and microservices. It covers the creation, structure, common use cases, and potential drawbacks of JWTs, as well as a step-by-step guide to implement JWT for authentication in a Spring Boot application.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3bc8dcf919d72e7744dc4e86ad14accd?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":24,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"bZKb437ru","title":"Creating and Publishing an NPM Package with Automated Versioning and Deployment","url":"https://reflectoring.io/create-and-publish-npm-package/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/creating-and-publishing-an-npm-package-with-automated-versioning-and-deployment-bzkb437ru","summary":"A step-by-step guide to creating and publishing an NPM package using TypeScript. Covers setting up Node.js, initializing helper packages, writing package functions and tests, publishing to NPM, automating publishing with GitHub Actions and Changesets, and using the package.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/336ade6f556d9438d1b4f45e17e65bf6?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-15T13:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"8a6XnTyj1","title":"Offloading File Transfers with Amazon S3 Presigned URLs in Spring Boot","url":"https://reflectoring.io/offloading-file-transfers-with-amazon-s3-presigned-urls-in-spring-boot/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/offloading-file-transfers-with-amazon-s3-presigned-urls-in-spring-boot-8a6xntyj1","summary":"Learn how to offload file transfers from an application server to the client using Presigned URLs in a Spring Boot application. These time-limited URLs allow for secure uploads and downloads directly to/from a storage solution like Amazon S3.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5ceeb0ec68d0146606352ea5e2983a7a?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-14T18:30:00.000Z"},{"id":"bFcusl2XE","title":"One Stop Guide to Java Functional Interfaces","url":"https://reflectoring.io/one-stop-guide-to-java-functional-interfaces/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/one-stop-guide-to-java-functional-interfaces-bfcusl2xe","summary":"Introduction to Java functional programming, lambda expressions, functional interfaces, and custom functional interfaces. Explains the advantages and disadvantages of functional programming in Java.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea0250d3c52676e9cb133941f97f7cb2?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-10T13:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"6k7wBgg6U","title":"Apache HttpClient Configuration","url":"https://reflectoring.io/apache-http-client-config/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/apache-httpclient-configuration-6k7wbgg6u","summary":"Learn how to configure Apache HttpClient for web communication, optimize connection management, enable caching, and customize request and response interceptors.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a6bcc858c50f5bea32f82d1c2b6e0fc4?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-28T13:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"eTPSWVADh","title":"Classic APIs Offered by Apache HttpClient","url":"https://reflectoring.io/apache-http-client-classic-apis/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/classic-apis-offered-by-apache-httpclient-etpswvadh","summary":"Learn about the classic APIs offered by Apache HttpClient for sending and receiving data over the internet in synchronous mode. Explore examples of HTTP and CRUD operations, processing HTTP responses, executing and testing HTTP methods, and using user-defined types in request processing.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/391f424b6d605166199653d8f82196a0?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-28T13:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"Znuum1637","title":"Create a HTTP Client with Apache HttpClient","url":"https://reflectoring.io/create-a-http-client-with-apache-http-client/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/create-a-http-client-with-apache-httpclient-znuum1637","summary":"Learn about Apache HttpClient and its role in web communication. Understand the importance of HTTP clients and their role in fetching data from the internet. Explore the features and capabilities of Apache HttpClient and how it simplifies HTTP communication in Java applications.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/395701e4a4555fb596c37fbf73dc9f26?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-28T13:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"6CjAY15E4","title":"Reactive APIs Offered by Apache HttpClient","url":"https://reflectoring.io/apache-http-client-reactive-apis/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/reactive-apis-offered-by-apache-httpclient-6cjay15e4","summary":"This post explores the reactive APIs offered by Apache HttpClient, their advantages, and how to use them in combination with RxJava for asynchronous HTTP communication. It also compares the async and reactive APIs and provides guidance on choosing the right approach for different scenarios.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/9deff8e1123c2a21750cb0d51d1a2a9a?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-28T13:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"7fA13Uonp","title":"Async APIs Offered by Apache HttpClient","url":"https://reflectoring.io/apache-http-client-async-apis/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/async-apis-offered-by-apache-httpclient-7fa13uonp","summary":"Learn about the async APIs offered by Apache HttpClient and how to use them for web communication. Explore the different categories of APIs provided by Apache HttpClient. Understand the purpose of starting and stopping the HTTP async client.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/40e6da67264237421c67e23285a7d034?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-28T13:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["neontech","growwengg","devgenius","earthly","pointer"],"opposite_handles":["sphaerophoria","developervoices","codewithantonio","goto","webdevcody"],"similar":[{"id":"neontech","handle":"neontech","name":"Neon","is_squad":false,"x":-3.2108,"y":4.6044,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":350,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--65EDghou--/f_auto/v1724339118/logos/neontech","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":3.931554,"median_upvotes":2.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.004286,"avg_read_time":5.625714,"tag_diversity":0.457143},"top_tags_preview":[["postgresql",238],["database",116],["cloud",82]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[6.5588,-1.8676],"cadence_depth":[7.2059,-0.6765],"hype_variety":[-1.9853,5.0588],"title_style":[0.9412,0.1471]}},{"id":"growwengg","handle":"growwengg","name":"Groww Engineering","is_squad":false,"x":-3.0008,"y":4.7685,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":42,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/imag